messages:
olivia: Quick architecture question — think we should add a 'promoted pinned' fast-path + a 'soft-reserve' reclaim in the allocator for long-running streaming workloads? Trying to balance spike latency vs fragmentation. TL;DR: pin until end-of-seq vs short-lived soft reservations.
amar: +1 to discussing. can you sketch the API shape? is this per-tenant or global pool? :thinking:
olivia: idea: allocator exposes
```
// reserve a small soft slot that can be preempted under pressure
int soft_reserve(size_t bytes, uint64_t lease_ms);
// promote an allocation to pinned (non-evictable) until seq finishes
int pin_until(uint64_t seq_id);
// hint to reclaim voluntarily
void reclaim_hint(int alloc_id);
```
and a configurable policy: max_soft_percent, promotion_cost_threshold
kevin: careful: pin_until needs strong invariants or we'll leak pinned pages -> OOM. need accounting + auto-release on seq timeout. add `pin_guard` that auto-unpins after X ms.
olivia: agreed — we should also require callers to provide `seq_id` and register a finalizer. auto-unpin fallback on timeout + metric `pin_leaks`
runtime-bot: [deploy] canary rollout started for `allocator-soft-reserve-v2` at 10% traffic
sylvia: tradeoffs: promoted pins reduce page churn but harm fair-sharing. suggest tiered-retention: only allow promotion if tenant_usage < tenant_promotion_limit and global_pinned_ratio < 15%.
amar: also consider compaction window: when fragmentation goes above threshold, trigger background compaction. compaction can coalesce soft-reserves first. cost vs latency tradeoff.
kevin: telemetry we need: promotion_rate, promotion_failures, soft_reserve_preemptions, avg_promoted_lifetime, fragmentation_ratio_95p. also add a perf test using long-stream with varying seq lengths.
nate: for rollout, propose canary plan: 10% -> 25% -> 50% with perf gates: p95 latency regression < 5%, memory overhead < 2% of baseline. define synthetic workload in e2e harness.
olivia: sounds good. action items: (1) I’ll draft an RFC with API + config knobs + metrics, (2) kevin will draft perf harness, (3) sylvia to list tenant policy thresholds. will attach a simple patch in RFC for pin_guard and `soft_reserve` behavior. thanks :party:
